                            <comment id="505196" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:45:06 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Uploaded the standalone fix: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70464" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70464&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21126" title="shutdown_node_hard overwrites caller loop variable" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21126"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-21126&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: keep hard shutdown retry counter local). Four focused RHEL 9.8 checks using the actual helper with power operations stubbed fail before the fix and pass after it: caller counter preservation on immediate success, retry success and exhaustion, plus absence of a global counter leak. Retry counts and return codes remain correct. Bash syntax, checkpatch and two local review rounds passed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="505211" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:22:55 +0000">&lt;p&gt;At Patrick Farrell request, the one-line shutdown retry counter fix from change 70464 is folded into change 69332 patchset 10: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69332/10" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69332/10&lt;/a&gt; . Closing this separate tracking ticket; the fix is now tracked under &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20157" title="deadlock between recovery and IO" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20157"&gt;LU-20157&lt;/a&gt;. Four focused RHEL 9.8 checks fail before the fix and pass after it, covering caller counter preservation and global leakage with unchanged retry counts and return codes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
